ertilizer for paddy in clay soil? · 11:54 AM · 🌾 **Paddy in Clay / Heavy Soils:** • **Basal Dose:** Apply 50% Nitrogen (Urea), full dose of Single Super Phosphate (SSP 60kg/ha), 75% MOP, and 25 kg Zinc Sulfate/ha during final puddling. • **Top Dressing:** 25% Nitrogen at active tillering (21-25 days) + 25% Nitrogen at panicle initiation. • **Water Management:** Maintain 3-5 cm standing water during vegetative tillering. Drain 10 days before harvest. · 11:54 AM · What is the best fertilizer for paddy in clay soil? · 11:54 AM · 🌾 **Paddy in Clay / Heavy Soils:** • **Basal Dose:** Apply 50% Nitrogen (Urea), full dose of Single Super Phosphate (SSP 60kg/ha), 75% MOP, and 25 kg Zinc Sulfate/ha during final puddling. • **Top Dressing:** 25% Nitrogen at active tillering (21-25 days) + 25% Nitrogen at panicle initiation. • **Water Management:** Maintain 3-5 cm standing water during vegetative tillering. Drain 10 days before harvest. · 11:54 AM\n  - form:\n    - textbox \"Ask about fertilizers, pest remedies, crop rotation, soil health...\" [ref=e133]\n    - button \"Voice Input (Speech-to-Text)\" [active] [ref=e134] [cursor=pointer]\n    - button \"Send Message\" [ref=e135] [cursor=pointer]\n  - text: AI Agronomist provides guidance based on ICAR and agricultural research datasets. For severe localized outbreaks, consult your local Krishi Vigyan Kendra (KVK).\n</untrusted_page_content>","media":[{"mime_type":"image/png","uri":"file:///C:/Users/abasu/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8280cdb4-257b-4bb7-95c6-bfaa06859e23/.system_generated/logs/media/step_30_media_0.png"}]}
