e113] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e114] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: March - April\n        - heading \"Harvest & Post-Harvest\" [level=4]\n        - text: Harvest wheat and mustard in early morning to prevent pod shattering. Store grains under 11% moisture.\n        - generic [ref=e115] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e116] [offscreen]\n      - text: Agronomist's Golden Rule · Never miss the 1st irrigation in wheat at 21 days (Crown Root Initiation stage).\n    - generic:\n      - text: March to June · Watermelon, Muskmelon, Cucumber, Okra (Bhindi), Moong (Green Gram), Fodder Cowpea\n      - heading \"Zaid Season (Short Summer / Pre-Monsoon)\" [level=3]\n      - generic:\n        - text: February - March\n        - heading \"Land Preparation\" [level=4]\n        - text: Prepare high raised beds or pits with enriched vermicompost for cucurbit vines.\n        - generic [ref=e117] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e118] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: March\n        - heading \"Sowing & Nursery\" [level=4]\n        - text: Sow seeds in warm soil with plastic mulch to conserve precious soil moisture and suppress weeds.\n        - generic [ref=e119] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e120] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: April - May\n        - heading \"Irrigation & Nutrients\" [level=4]\n        - text: Frequent light drip irrigations every 3-4 days during peak summer heat to prevent fruit dropping.\n        - generic [ref=e121] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e122] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: May - June\n        - heading \"Harvest & Post-Harvest\" [level=4]\n        - text: Harvest melons when ground spot turns creamy yellow and tendril withers; harvest early morning